/*
 * apex_board.h
 *
 * Board-level helpers, and the one header the rest of the project can
 * include to reach everything.
 *
 * WHERE THE PIN NAMES COME FROM
 *
 *   The _Pin and _GPIO_Port macros used below are generated by CubeMX
 *   into Core/Inc/main.h, from the User Labels set on each pin in the
 *   .ioc file. Nothing here hard-codes a pin number, so the .ioc remains
 *   the single source of truth for the pin map: change a label there,
 *   regenerate, and this follows automatically.
 *
 * WHY THE POLARITY HELPERS EXIST
 *
 *   Two signals on this board are ACTIVE LOW -- the pin must be driven
 *   low to make the thing happen. Every caller that had to remember
 *   which ones would eventually get one wrong, so the polarity is
 *   written down once, here, and nothing else is allowed to know it.
 *
 * THE FOLDER LAYOUT
 *
 *     board/     this file, and the unit conventions
 *     drivers/   the peripherals: encoder, bridge, sensors, USB
 *     comms/     framing, protocols, and the command handlers
 *     control/   the control loop and what runs inside it
 *     motion/    things that drive the motor: spin, calibrate, measure
 *     monitor/   telemetry and the protection supervisor
 */

